A regular customer came into the cafe.
He ordered a coffee.
I went near the coffee machine.
Sunita had taught me everything just a while ago.
Still, I was learning to use the machine.
This was my first coffee.
I started to heat the milk.
But I did not get the timing right.
The milk got too hot.
It spilled out of the container.
My first coffee came out completely wrong.
I got very nervous.
Sunita immediately came near me.
She said to me affectionately, "Maya, no problem."
She calmly cleaned up all that mess.
Then she quickly made a perfect coffee herself.
She gave that hot coffee to the customer.
He smiled and took the coffee.
